<main id="main"><div class="container"><nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="index.html">Home</a></li><li aria-current="page"><span>Cash-Out Refinance in Miami</span></li></ol></nav></div><section class="hero"><div class="container hero-grid"><div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Home equity strategy</p><h1>Cash-Out Refinance in Miami</h1><p>Explore cash-out refinance options for Miami homeowners who want to access equity, consolidate debt, renovate, or restructure financing.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="start.html">Review Cash-Out Options</a><a class="btn btn-secondary" href="mortgage-calculator-florida.html">Estimate Refinance Payment</a></div><div class="trust-row"><span class="trust-pill">Matthew Gromadzki</span><span class="trust-pill">NMLS #2560919</span><span class="trust-pill">Miami · Florida</span><span class="trust-pill">Call (305) 988-4806</span></div></div><div class="hero-panel rate-card"><div class="rate-item"><span>Best first step</span><strong>Preapproval</strong></div><div class="rate-item"><span>Core review</span><strong>Payment + cash to close</strong></div><div class="rate-item"><span>Miami focus</span><strong>Condo + jumbo checks</strong></div><a class="btn btn-primary full" href="start.html">Send Scenario</a></div></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container two-col"><article class="prose"><p>A cash-out refinance replaces your existing mortgage with a new loan that may provide cash back at closing, depending on equity and eligibility. It can be useful, but it should be compared carefully against alternatives.</p><p>The right decision depends on equity, credit, income, loan-to-value, property type, occupancy, current rate, new rate, and closing costs.</p><h2>Common cash-out goals</h2><p>Miami homeowners may explore cash-out refinancing for renovations, reserves, debt consolidation, investment property down payments, business liquidity, or restructuring expensive debts.</p><p>A mortgage review should compare total monthly obligations, not just the mortgage payment.</p><h2>Condo cash-out review</h2><p>If the property is a condo, the association and building may still affect available loan options. Insurance, reserves, litigation, and assessments can matter during underwriting.</p><p>Review these issues early if timing is important.</p></article><aside><form class="lead-form lead-form-compact" method="post" action="quote.html" data-lead-form><h2>Request a Cash-Out Refinance Miami Quote</h2><p>Answer a few basics and we’ll review the best mortgage path for your scenario.</p><input type="hidden" name="source_page" value="preview"><label>Loan goal<select name="loan_goal" required><option value="">Select one</option><option>Buying a home</option><option>Refinancing</option><option>Cash-out refinance</option><option>Investment property</option><option>Condo financing</option></select></label><div class="form-row"><label>Purchase price / value<input name="property_value" inputmode="numeric" placeholder="$650,000"></label><label>Down payment / equity<input name="down_payment" inputmode="numeric" placeholder="$100,000"></label></div><div class="form-row"><label>Credit score range<select name="credit_score"><option value="">Select range</option><option>760+</option><option>720–759</option><option>680–719</option><option>640–679</option><option>Below 640</option><option>Not sure</option></select></label><label>Property city<input name="property_city" placeholder="Miami"></label></div><div class="form-row"><label>Name<input name="name" autocomplete="name" required></label><label>Phone<input name="phone" autocomplete="tel" required></label></div><label>Email<input name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" required></label><button class="btn btn-primary full" type="submit">Start Mortgage Review</button><p class="form-note">No obligation. Mortgage options depend on underwriting, lender guidelines, property type, and documentation.</p></form></aside></div></section><section class="section soft"><div class="container"><div class="cta-band"><div><p class="eyebrow">Fast next step</p><h2>Get a mortgage scenario review before you make a decision.</h2><p>Send purchase price, down payment, credit range, income type, and property city. The goal is to compare real options, not guess based on generic rates.</p></div><div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="start.html">Start Review</a><a class="btn btn-secondary" href="tel:+13059884806">Call (305) 988-4806</a></div></div></div></section><section class="section faq-section"><div class="container narrow"><p class="eyebrow">Questions</p><h2>Cash-Out Refinance in Miami FAQ</h2><div class="faq-list"><details><summary>How much cash can I take out?</summary><p>The amount depends on property value, current mortgage balance, loan-to-value limits, credit, income, property type, and the chosen program.</p></details><details><summary>Is a cash-out refinance better than a HELOC?</summary><p>It depends on rate, term, costs, how much equity you need, and how long you plan to keep the financing. Compare both when available.</p></details><details><summary>Can investment properties use cash-out refinancing?</summary><p>Possibly. Investment property cash-out options have different requirements than primary residence refinances.</p></details></div></div></section><section class="section related-section"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">Keep comparing</p><h2>Related mortgage pages</h2><div class="card-grid small-grid"><a class="mini-card" href="refinance-mortgage-miami.html">Refinance Mortgage Miami<span>→</span></a><a class="mini-card" href="investment-property-loans-miami.html">Investment Property Loans Miami<span>→</span></a><a class="mini-card" href="dscr-loans-miami.html">DSCR Loans Miami<span>→</span></a><a class="mini-card" href="miami-mortgage-rates.html">Miami Mortgage Rates<span>→</span></a></div></div></section></main>
